      <Description>Delibera — Thoughtful AI Decisions. A framework for collective decision making through structured AI deliberation. v10.4.0 is the API-truth release and carries ONE BREAKING CHANGE: IDebateStrategy.ExecuteAsync takes Func&lt;DebateRound, CancellationToken, ValueTask&gt;? instead of Action&lt;DebateRound&gt;? for onRoundCompleted, because a synchronous callback pinned a thread-pool thread for the duration of every per-round checkpoint write and repackaged OperationCanceledException as AggregateException. The public CouncilExecutor.OnRoundCompleted event is unchanged and existing subscribers keep working. Platform surface: the IDebateOrchestrator abstraction for distributed debate execution (in-process and Redis-backed), a pluggable result-caching layer (in-memory, file, Redis) with per-debate behavior control, and removed deprecated APIs (Moderator→Chairman, ModelCapabilities non-nullable, VectorStoreFactory, DebateStatus/DebateOrchestrationStatus dead values). Performance &amp; integrity: timer-based eviction of completed debate entries, IDisposable on internal caches, volatile int backing for cross-thread status, ConcurrentDictionary throughout, ConfigureAwait(false) library-wide, ValueTask on synchronous cache/store paths, ArrayPool buffers on the debate cache-key and text-similarity paths, and a rule-based model-context-window lookup (exact pattern first, then longest matching substring) instead of the previous order-dependent enumeration. Full feature set: multi-model councils with RAG (Qdrant, PgVector), debate strategies, Knowledge Keeper, Chairman roles, dependency injection, context compression, AutoChunking (progressive disclosure for large documents), Microsoft.Extensions.Logging, Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience (Polly v8 retry pipelines), IHttpClientFactory wiring, response-language enforcement, parallel Operator requests, async streaming council (IAsyncEnumerable&lt;DebateRound&gt;), pluggable voting engine (Majority/BordaCount/Weighted), debate persistence &amp; resume via checkpoints, agent memory (in-memory/Qdrant/pgvector), OpenTelemetry-style observability (spans + metrics), structured JSON output (schema-validated verdicts with retry), adaptive strategy switching on stagnation, debate templates &amp; presets library, multi-modal attachments via IFileContentReader, HTML export, debate timeout, persona presets, benchmark mode, and participant limit guard.</Description>
